# social_jira4 REAL RUN — top-10 fabrication-qualifying prompts x seeds 7,8 x 4 models.
#
# ONE JOB PER MODEL via `queue MODEL in`, so the four progress simultaneously instead of summing
# their very different runtimes (measured per rollout tonight: gemma ~13 min, kimi ~13, glm ~5,
# deepseek ~23). Within each job the 20 (prompt, seed) rollouts also fan out, 4 at a time.
#
# WHAT RUNS. 10 prompts (first 10 records of reports/v4_dspro_fabrication_qualifying.jsonl,
# score-ordered 6.33 -> 1.67, 10 distinct prompt_sha), each replayed at seeds 7 and 8. Prompt index
# becomes the step, so runs/step000..step009 each hold two seeds — the shape a real optimizer run
# writes, which the viewer reads without reinterpretation.
#
# 10 x 2 x 4 = 80 rollouts. No prompter, no meta-gate, no consistency gate, no fabrication judge:
# the prompts are fixed and each already cleared the dspro fabrication gate when it was mined.
# Only CATEGORY / SOUNDNESS / AT-STAKE run, on deepseek-v4-pro.
#
# CONCURRENCY. --workers 4 rollouts x --critic-workers 4 judge threads = up to 16 in-flight calls
# per job, ~64 across the four. The two multiply, which is why both are bounded; peak is well under
# the 8-concurrent-job precedent from the v4h campaign (3655 judge calls, no rate-limit failures).
# Providers are pinned to VERIFIED ordered lists (see the config header) — a single pin was tried
# and rejected: ~300 calls per model on one upstream with fallback off returns 429 rather than
# rerouting, which three preflight sweeps demonstrated by rate-limiting DeepInfra outright.
#
# qwen3.6-27b IS ABSENT — it drops the forced tool call on 40-60% of calls and the cause is still
# open. A dropped post is silent: the turn completes, nothing is posted, and the transcript reads as
# a model declining to argue. It gets its own job once its tool rate is verified at n>=10.
#
# COST. Measured from tonight's rollouts: ~$0.40/rollout judging + ~$0.07 generation -> ~$38 for
# 80 rollouts, rising toward $55 if prompts run the full four planning rounds. Judging is ~85%.
#
# CPU-ONLY. Submit with `condor_submit_bid 25`.
executable = /fast/jtaraz/LIARS/colosseum-detection/experiments/social_jira4/cluster/run_sj4_fixedprompt.sh
arguments  = "--step-files experiments/social_jira4/outputs/v4d_mg1_fabrication_dspro/steps/step_023.json,experiments/social_jira4/outputs/v4d_mg1_fabrication_dspro/steps/step_033.json,experiments/social_jira4/outputs/v4d_mg1_fabrication_dspro/steps/step_018.json,experiments/social_jira4/outputs/v4e_mg2_fabrication_dspro/steps/step_037.json,experiments/social_jira4/outputs/v4d_mg1_fabrication_dspro/steps/step_035.json,experiments/social_jira4/outputs/v4g_fabrication_dspro_a/steps/step_003.json,experiments/social_jira4/outputs/v4h_fabrication_dspro_c_gptoss/steps/step_001.json,experiments/social_jira4/outputs/v4h_fabrication_dspro_d_gptoss/steps/step_002.json,experiments/social_jira4/outputs/v4e_mg2_fabrication_dspro/steps/step_033.json,experiments/social_jira4/outputs/v4d_mg1_fabrication_dspro/steps/step_019.json --config experiments/social_jira4/configs/social_jira4_realrun_pinned_or.yaml --out-dir experiments/social_jira4/outputs/rr10_$(MODEL) --models or-$(MODEL) --seeds 7,8 --workers 4 --critic-workers 4"

output = /fast/jtaraz/LIARS/colosseum-detection/experiments/social_jira4/cluster/rr10_$(MODEL).out
error  = /fast/jtaraz/LIARS/colosseum-detection/experiments/social_jira4/cluster/rr10_$(MODEL).err
log    = /fast/jtaraz/LIARS/colosseum-detection/experiments/social_jira4/cluster/rr10_$(MODEL).log

request_cpus   = 4
request_memory = 8192
request_disk   = 4G

queue MODEL in (kimi-k2.6, glm-5.2, gemma-4-31b, deepseek-v4-flash)
